are, and containers, as well as insulated bowls and food jars, ceramic-lined mugs and stackable cups, French presses, pitchers, wine chillers, wine tumblers, the beverage bucket, colsters, and cocktail shakers; and cookware. Further, the company provides apparel, such as hats, shirts, and sweatshirts, as well as ice substitutes and other YETI branded products. It sells its products through its direct-to-consumer channel, including websites, corporate sales programs, and retail stores, as well as through its wholesale channel. YETI Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","employees":1390,"website":"https://www.yeti.com","country":"United States","city":"Austin","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Martin H. Duff IV","title":"Senior VP, Chief Supply Chain & Operations Officer"},{"name":"Mr. Bryan C. Barksdale J.D.","title":"Senior VP, Chief Legal Officer & Secretary"},{"name":"Mr. Arvind  Bhatia C.F.A.","title":"Vice President of Investor Relations"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":14.65,"tpe":19.21,"ps":1.252,"pfcf":18.23,"peg":1.15,"pb":2.925,"ev_ebitda":11.78,"rev_growth":0.057,"eps_growth":0.174,"eps_growth_fwd":0.1136,"eps_growth_next":0.1239,"div_yield":0.00755,"roe":0.1543,"roa":0.06135,"de":109.2,"gross_margin":0.3804,"op_margin":0.09768,"profit_margin":0.05785,"current_ratio":1.444},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":13.02,"sector":14.65,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":19.15,"sector":19.21,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":1.646,"sector":1.252,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"pfcf","label":"Price / FCF","v":25.01,"sector":18.23,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"peg","label":"PEG","v":1.27,"sector":1.15,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"pb","label":"Price / Book","v":5.228,"sector":2.925,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"de","label":"Debt / Equity (%)","v":41.52,"sector":109.2,"verdict":"Low debt"},{"k":"rev_growth","label":"Revenue growth","v":0.085,"sector":0.057,"verdict":"Strong